  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary path",
      "items": [
        "The consumer calls runScrape with searchParams, scraperOptions, onProgress and an AbortSignal; only the search keyword is required.",
        "buildSearchUrl sends only the fields that were set; runScrape launches Chromium, opens the search context and navigates.",
        "validateSearchNavigation rejects a missing response, an HTTP error, or a landing page off the guest search path.",
        "Discovery scrolls one list item at a time, then clicks See more jobs, until unique and raw card counts stop growing.",
        "Each distinct posting is clicked once and read only after the detail pane shows that posting's own ID.",
        "The company lookup adds companyAddresses; ScrapeOutcome returns to the caller."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why two browser contexts",
      "items": [
        "LinkedIn serves a company page's Locations section only to a cookie jar that has not yet seen a company page.",
        "So company pages load in their own context and clearCookies runs before every goto: 54 of 54 companies versus 1 of 54 on a reused context.",
        "The search context keeps its guest session; clearing it would end the job search mid-run.",
        "fetch() gets HTTP 999 from LinkedIn, so a company page must really be navigated to."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Guards and recovery",
      "items": [
        "Overlay ladder: pick a dismiss control, press Escape, then neutralize the overlay; the initial clear, See more clicks and every in-job click use it.",
        "Identity gate: the detail pane must match the card's job ID; one immediate re-click, then a DetailPaneIdentityError failure.",
        "Stale and identity-failed jobs get one deferred retry pass after the whole list was scraped once.",
        "The company lookup never rejects: a null means unreadable, an empty list means read and unpublished, and empty pages get emptyRetries (default 1)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Budgets and cancellation",
      "items": [
        "perJobTimeoutMs (default 45 s) clamps every wait inside one job instead of racing it.",
        "maxRunDurationMs becomes an AbortSignal: the run resolves with stoppedEarly set to run-time-budget and keeps its results.",
        "A caller abort rejects with ScrapeAbortedError carrying partial results; the browser still closes in finally."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Progress and diagnostics",
      "items": [
        "onProgress emits jobs:loading, jobs:found, job:start, then job:done or job:stale per job, plus overlay:undismissed.",
        "Stale diagnostics are collected per job and summarized into ScrapeOutcome.staleReport (on by default)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Ownership and trust",
      "items": [
        "The library is in-process: no server, database or files. The consuming app owns storage and scheduling.",
        "runScrape launches Chromium and closes it, and the company lookup's context, in its finally block.",
        "LinkedIn is an unofficial, moving surface with no login or credentials; markup and anti-bot gating vary by session.",
        "No search default is baked in: every field except the keyword is optional and every timing constant is overridable."
      ]
    }
  ]
